  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the END TB Strategy in Honduras - Honduras (01-Jan-2017-31-Jul-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Honduras, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Health of the Republic of Honduras (MOH)This program has the following goals: Detect at least 85&#x252c;&#xe1;percent of TB patients by 2020, in line with WHO estimates..  Reduce TB mortality by 25 percent in 2020 compared to 2015.. The objectives of this program are: Develop TB prevention and control activities for vulnerable populations.  Improve clinical and programmatic management of MDR-TB..  Improve implementation of quality DOTS strategy in the patient-centered TB comprehensive care and prevention framework..  Strengthen the comprehensive approach to TB/HIV co-infection..  Strengthen the laboratory network to improve diagnosis and the response to the new challenges proposed in the Stop TB strategy.</narrative>
  </description>
